NNAAMMEE
     mmkkccssmmaappppeerr — generates hashed conversion data for iconv(3)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     mmkkccssmmaappppeerr [--dd] [--mm | --pp] [--oo _o_u_t_f_i_l_e] [_i_n_f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmkkccssmmaappppeerr utility generates binary conversion data from plain text
     conversion tables for the iconv(3) library.  The conversion data has two
     components: The conversion mapping between specific character encodings.
     A pivot file, which the possible source and destination encoding pairs or
     the set of mappings to use for a compound encoding.

     The following options are available:

     --dd            Turns on debug mode.

     --mm            Generate mapping data from _i_n_f_i_l_e.

     --oo _o_u_t_f_i_l_e    Put generated binary data to _o_u_t_f_i_l_e.

     --pp            Generate pivot data from _o_u_t_f_i_l_e.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The mmkkccssmmaappppeerr utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     iconv(1), mkesdb(1), iconv(3)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     mmkkccssmmaappppeerr first appeared in NetBSD 2.0, and made its appearance in
     FreeBSD 9.0.

